@startuml
title Risk & Churn — as-built lifecycle: classify-at-sync (write) + read paths

participant "SyncService /\nLedgerRebuilder" as Sync
participant "RiskEngine\n(risk_engine.go)" as Eng
database "SubscriptionRepo\n(risk_state column)" as SubRepo
participant "SnapshotProcessor" as Snap
database "daily_metrics_snapshot" as SnapDB

== Write path (once per sync, deterministic) ==
Sync -> Eng : ClassifyAll(subs, now)
Eng -> Eng : per sub -> ClassifyRisk\nterminal->CHURNED · FROZEN->1cycle · PENDING->SAFE\nACTIVE+future/nil->SAFE · else daysPastDue 30/60/90
Eng --> Sync : subs[].RiskState set (in place)
Sync -> SubRepo : UpsertBatch (persist risk_state)
Sync -> Snap : BackfillHistoricalSnapshots + RefreshTodaySnapshot
Snap -> SubRepo : read persisted states
Snap -> SnapDB : counts (Safe/1c/2c/Churned) + RevenueAtRiskCents + RenewalSuccessRate

== Read paths (NEVER re-run the engine — RISK-1b) ==
actor Partner as U
participant "risk/churn/retention\nhandlers" as H
U -> H : GET /risk/summary | /reports/churn | /reports/retention
H -> SubRepo : FindByAppID / FindByRiskState (persisted states)
H -> SnapDB : trend series (+ renewal rate headline)
note right of H
  Risk Summary: distribution + ranked at-risk stores (persisted)
  Churn: LIVE count of CHURNED subs (may drift vs snapshot)
  Retention: renewal rate from SNAPSHOT ; reactivations from events
  Revenue at Risk: recoverable = 1c*0.60 + 2c*0.25 (hardcoded)
end note
H --> U : JSON (+ optional CSV)

note over Eng
  DIVERGENCES: PAUSED falls through to ACTIVE-days logic
  UTC-only days math (no DST) · recovery constants unvalidated
end note
@enduml
